  "Question": "If an angle of a triangle remains unchanged but each of its two including sides is doubled, then the area is multiplied by:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(3\\)",
    "C": "\\(4\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "more than \\(6\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Both sides enclosing the unchanged angle have been multiplied by \\(2\\). The two triangles are therefore similar by the side-angle-side similarity criterion, with length scale factor \\(2\\).\n\nA corresponding base and altitude are both doubled. Since triangle area is one-half base times altitude, the area is multiplied by\n\\[\n2\\cdot2=4.\n\\]\nThe answer is C.",
